    {
      "name": "12 — WebSocket Reference",
      "description": "Socket.io events emitted by the server. These cannot be tested via HTTP — use the Socket.io test client or integrate with the React dashboard.\n\n**Connect:** socket.io client → http://localhost:5000\n\n**Events emitted by server:**\n\n| Event | Trigger | Payload |\n|---|---|---|\n| signal:new | New BUY/WAIT/SKIP signal saved | Signal document |\n| signal:update | Signal isActive toggled | { signalId, isActive } |\n| market:update | Market data refreshed | Market snapshot |\n| trade:target1 | PATCH /:id/target1 called | Trade document |\n| trade:target2 | Trade closed with TARGET2 | Trade document |\n| trade:sl_warning | Price within 2% above SL | { tradeId, symbol, currentPrice, stopLoss, distancePct } |\n| trade:earnings | Stock within 15 days of earnings | { symbol, daysToEarnings } |\n| market:bearmode | Nifty drops below 20 EMA | {} |\n| market:vixspike | VIX exceeds 25 | { vix } |\n| scan:complete | Full scan cycle finishes | { scanned, signals, timestamp } |\n\n**Quick test (browser console):**\n```javascript\nconst s = io('http://localhost:5000');\ns.onAny((event, data) => console.log(event, data));\n```",
